# Mandao guide

This workspace uses [Mandao](https://www.npmjs.com/package/mandao) for spec-driven development.
Every command is a *mandao*: invoke it as `/mandao-<command>` in your agent (Codex: `$mandao-<command>`).

Flow: `constitution` → `story` → `specify` → `[clarify]` → `tasks` → `implement` → `verify` → `close`

## Workspace

- Mode: `monorepo`
- Specs: `specs/<id>-<slug>/` (id from the tracker, or a sequential `NNN` when there is none)
- Workspace constitution: `docs/constitution/`; each project may extend it in `<project>/docs/constitution/`

| Project | Path | Profile |
|---|---|---|
| api | `services/api` | app |
| assistant | `services/assistant` | ai |

## Commands

- `/mandao-init` — Initialize Mandao in this repository.
- `/mandao-specify <spec> [--hotfix] [depth]` — Turn an approved story into requirements and design.
  - `<spec>`: Spec id, e.g. PROJ-1-login
  - `--hotfix`: A production fix
  - `<depth>` (default `standard`): lite | standard | full

Not implemented yet: `/mandao-evals`, `/mandao-tasks`.

## Terminal commands

The commands above run every other script themselves. These are the ones you type (`mandao <command> --help` lists the flags; `docs/cli.md` in the Mandao repository has the full index):

- `mandao init` — set up Mandao in a workspace
- `mandao sync` — regenerate the harness files from `.mandao/config.yml`
- `mandao doctor` — check the configuration, the generated files and the optional tools
- `mandao update` — apply the installed Mandao version
- `mandao harness add` — generate files for another harness
- `mandao skills list` — list the pinned skills
- `mandao skills add` — install, verify and pin catalog skills
- `mandao skills restore` — restore missing skills from the lock
- `mandao models` — show the model of each role
- `mandao models set` — choose the model of a role
- `mandao models mode` — simple or routed models
- `mandao models profile` — peak, balanced or economy models
- `mandao approve` — approve a step from the terminal, without a model session
- `mandao deliver` — push, PR and merge after green CI (the agent runs it in the session too)
- `mandao worktree list` — the spec worktrees and whether they were merged
- `mandao worktree clean` — remove merged worktrees that hold no work
- `mandao intake close` — close an intake proposal
- `mandao intake clean` — delete the extracted text of closed intakes
- `mandao run cost` — spend per command and role
- `mandao run version-notes` — release notes of a version

## Rules

- Never invent context. Mark gaps as `ASSUMPTION`, `OPEN` or `CONFLICT`, always with the source.
- If a code graph exists (e.g. graphify), query it before searching files.
- Write business content (story, release notes, questions to the PO, product context) in `en` and technical content (requirements, design, tasks, technical docs) in `en`. Section headings, keywords (GIVEN/WHEN/THEN, MUST, AC-n, FR-n) and markers stay in English. Code and commits are always in English.
- Spec status: `draft → approved → in-progress → blocked → verified → closed | abandoned`.
- A human approves every significant change and anything published outside the repository.
- Templates live in `.mandao/templates/<profile>/`; use the profile of the project you are working on.

## Commits

Subject: `<emoji> <type>(<scope>): <subject>`, imperative mood, at most 72 characters without the emoji.

Emoji per type: feat ✨, fix 🐛, docs 📝, style 🎨, refactor ♻️, test ✅, chore 🔧, perf ⚡️, build 📦️, ci 👷, revert ⏪️. A breaking change uses 💥 instead of the type emoji.

Trailers: `Refs: <tracker id>`, `Mandao-Task: <task>`, `Mandao-AC: <AC ids>`, `Mandao-Quick: <name>` for quick changes.
